## Phase 2: Foundational Infrastructure (Blocking Prerequisites)

**Purpose**: Core packages that all user stories depend on; MUST be complete before story implementation

**⚠️ CRITICAL**: No user story work can begin until this phase is complete

### Configuration & Logging

- [ ] T012 [P] Create `internal/logging/logger.go` with zap setup, JSON encoding, secret redaction function
  - Implement `NewLogger(level string) *zap.Logger`
  - Implement `redactSecret(s string) string` → returns `****{last4chars}`
  - Add custom encoder for sensitive fields
  - Unit tests: secret masking, JSON output validation

- [ ] T013 [P] Create `internal/config/models.go` with Config struct hierarchy
  - `Config` → `Auth`, `Client`, `Output`, `Watermark`, `Logging`
  - Include field tags for viper: `mapstructure`, `yaml`, `json`
  - Document defaults inline

- [ ] T014 [P] Create `internal/config/config.go` with Viper loading
  - `LoadConfig(configPath, flags)` → merges flags > env > file > defaults
  - Support YAML/TOML/JSON config files
  - Path expansion for `~/.lastfm/`, `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`
  - Return `*Config` or error

- [ ] T015 Create `internal/config/validation.go` with config validation
  - `ValidateConfig(cfg *Config)` → checks required fields (LASTFM_API_KEY, output target, Azure if needed)
  - Clear error messages for validation failures
  - Unit tests: valid configs pass, invalid configs fail with helpful errors

### Last.fm API Client (Core)

- [ ] T016 [P] Create `internal/lastfm/models.go` with data structures
  - `ScrobbleResponse` (from Last.fm API)
  - `Page` struct (results, page info, total)
  - Parse Last.fm API JSON response structure
  - Unit tests: JSON unmarshaling, edge cases (missing fields)

- [ ] T017 [P] Create `internal/lastfm/client.go` with HTTP client
  - `Client` struct: BaseURL, APIKey, Timeout, Limiter, RetryMax
  - `NewClient(config) *Client`
  - `FetchPage(ctx, username, from, until, pageNum, pageSize) (*Page, error)`
  - Implement retry logic (429, 5xx) with backoff (stub calls to ratelimit package)
  - Timeout enforcement per request
  - Unit tests: basic client creation, timeout handling (mock server)

- [ ] T018 [P] Create `internal/lastfm/pagination.go` with pagination helpers
  - `FilterNowPlaying(scrobbles) []Scrobble` → exclude entries without date.uts
  - `IsShortCircuit(page, watermark) bool` → check if 0 records with uts > watermark
  - Unit tests: filtering, short-circuit detection

### Rate Limiting & Retry

- [ ] T019 [P] Create `internal/ratelimit/limiter.go` with rate limiter
  - `Limiter` struct: wraps `golang.org/x/time/rate.Limiter`, backoff
  - `NewLimiter(qps int, maxRetries int) *Limiter`
  - `Wait(ctx)` → token bucket enforcement (sleep if needed)
  - Unit tests: QPS enforcement (measure time between calls), token distribution

- [ ] T020 [P] Create `internal/ratelimit/backoff.go` with retry strategy
  - `DoWithRetry(ctx, fn, maxRetries)` → exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, max 32s)
  - `ParseRetryAfter(headers)` → extract Retry-After header if present
  - `IsRetryable(err)` → classify errors (429, 5xx → true; others → false)
  - Unit tests: exponential sequence, max retries enforced, Retry-After honored

### Writer Interface & Local Implementation

- [ ] T021 [P] Create `internal/writer/writer.go` with Scrobble type and Writer interface
  - `Scrobble` struct: username, artist, track, album, uts, mbid, source, ingested_at, raw
  - `Writer` interface: `WriteBatch(ctx, records []Scrobble) error`, `Flush(ctx) error`, `Close(ctx) error`
  - JSON struct tags for NDJSON marshaling
  - Unit tests: struct marshaling to JSON

- [ ] T022 Create `internal/writer/local.go` with LocalWriter
  - `LocalWriter` struct: filepath, file handle, buffered writer, fsync behavior
  - `NewLocalWriter(filepath) (*LocalWriter, error)` → create or open existing file
  - `WriteBatch(ctx, records)` → write NDJSON (one JSON per line, buffered)
  - `Flush(ctx)` → flush buffer + fsync
  - `Close(ctx)` → cleanup, close file
  - Unit tests: append to file, fsync called, NDJSON format valid, error handling (permission denied)

### Watermark Store Interface & File Implementation

- [ ] T023 [P] Create `internal/watermark/store.go` with WatermarkStore interface and Watermark type
  - `Watermark` struct: username, max_uts, updated_at, sync_id
  - `WatermarkStore` interface: `Get(ctx, username) (uts int64, exists bool, err)`, `Put(ctx, username, uts) error`
  - Unit tests: interface definition

- [ ] T024 Create `internal/watermark/file.go` with FileStore
  - `FileStore` struct: base directory path
  - `NewFileStore(basePath) *FileStore`
  - `Get(ctx, username)` → read JSON watermark file `{basePath}/{username}.watermark`
  - `Put(ctx, username, uts)` → write atomically (temp file + rename)
  - Serialize watermark with updated_at timestamp and sync_id
  - Unit tests: read/write, atomic updates, missing file handling, concurrent access (file lock consideration)

### Azure Writer & Watermark Store (Stub Interfaces)

- [ ] T025 [P] Create `internal/writer/azure.go` with AzureWriter stub
  - Struct: temp dir, container client, prefix, username
  - `NewAzureWriter(container, prefix, username, tempDir) (*AzureWriter, error)`
  - `WriteBatch(ctx, records)` → write to temp file (reuse local writer pattern)
  - `Flush(ctx)` → upload temp file to Azure blob (path: `{prefix}dt=YYYY-MM-DD/{username}-HHMMSS.ndjson`)
  - `Close(ctx)` → delete temp file
  - Unit tests (integration): placeholder for Azurite tests

- [ ] T026 [P] Create `internal/watermark/azure.go` with AzureStore stub
  - Struct: container client, prefix
  - `NewAzureStore(container, prefix) *AzureStore`
  - `Get(ctx, username)` → read blob `{prefix}{username}.watermark`
  - `Put(ctx, username, uts)` → write blob with ETag concurrency check
  - Unit tests (integration): placeholder for Azurite tests

### CLI Framework & Command Skeleton

- [ ] T027 [P] Create `cmd/lastfm-sync/main.go` with cobra root command
  - Initialize cobra root cmd with version/help
  - Version injection from build flags
  - Global flags: `--log-level`, `--config-path`

- [ ] T028 [P] Create `cmd/lastfm-sync/commands/fetch.go` with fetch command skeleton
  - `NewFetchCmd()` → returns cobra.Command
  - Parse all CLI flags per plan (--user, --since, --until, --output, --azure-*, --qps, --timeout, etc.)
  - Stub: minimal Run function (to be filled in user story tasks)

- [ ] T029 [P] Create `cmd/lastfm-sync/commands/show-watermark.go`
  - Command to display current watermark for a user
  - Stub implementation (full in Polish phase)

- [ ] T030 [P] Create `cmd/lastfm-sync/commands/set-watermark.go`
  - Command to manually set watermark (recovery/migration)
  - Stub implementation

- [ ] T031 [P] Create `cmd/lastfm-sync/commands/version.go`
  - Display build info (version, build time, git commit)

### Test Utilities & Fixtures

- [ ] T032 [P] Create `pkg/testutil/fixtures.go` with mock data generators
  - `GenerateScrobbles(count int) []writer.Scrobble`
  - `MockLastfmPage(pageNum, pageSize int, maxUts int64) *lastfm.Page`
  - Helper to create mock HTTP responses

- [ ] T033 [P] Create `pkg/testutil/mocks.go` with mock implementations
  - `MockWriter` impl of `Writer` interface
  - `MockWatermarkStore` impl of `WatermarkStore` interface
  - `MockLastfmClient` impl (if needed for integration tests)

**Checkpoint**: Foundation complete. All user stories can now proceed in parallel.

