## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Initial Full Scrobble History Fetch (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: User can fetch complete Last.fm scrobble history to local NDJSON file in one run

**Independent Test**: Mock Last.fm API → run fetch → verify NDJSON output contains all records with correct format

### Tests for User Story 1 (TDD: Write First, Ensure Fail)

- [ ] T034 [P] [US1] Unit test: Last.fm client pagination in `internal/lastfm/client_test.go`
  - Test `FetchPage` with mock HTTP server returning paginated responses
  - Verify `from` parameter correctly passed
  - Verify page accumulation across multiple calls
  - Test boundary conditions (page 1, last page, single page)
  - Test "now playing" filtering

- [ ] T035 [P] [US1] Unit test: LocalWriter NDJSON output in `internal/writer/local_test.go`
  - Verify NDJSON format (one JSON per line)
  - Verify all fields present (username, artist, track, album, uts, mbid, source, ingested_at, raw)
  - Verify append behavior (multiple WriteBatch calls)
  - Verify file sync on flush

- [ ] T036 [P] [US1] Unit test: FileStore watermark in `internal/watermark/file_test.go`
  - Verify watermark file created after first sync
  - Verify watermark contains correct max_uts value
  - Verify atomic write (no corruption on crash)

- [ ] T037 [US1] Integration test: Full fetch → write → watermark flow in `cmd/lastfm-sync/integration_test.go`
  - Mock Last.fm API with 3 pages (200 records each)
  - Run `lastfm-sync fetch --user alice --output local --out-path /tmp/alice.ndjson`
  - Verify NDJSON file created with 600 records
  - Verify watermark file created with correct max_uts
  - Verify no duplicates (uniqueness check)

### Implementation for User Story 1

- [ ] T038 [US1] Implement Last.fm client retry middleware in `internal/lastfm/client.go`
  - Integrate `ratelimit.DoWithRetry` for resilience
  - Test with mock 429 response (verify retry + backoff)
  - Test with mock 5xx response (verify retry limit)

- [ ] T039 [US1] Complete LocalWriter implementation in `internal/writer/local.go`
  - Add `SetUsername(username string)` to track user (for ingested_at enrichment)
  - Verify NDJSON format compliance in tests

- [ ] T040 [US1] Complete FileStore implementation in `internal/watermark/file.go`
  - Atomic writes with temp file + rename
  - Error handling for file system issues

- [ ] T041 [US1] Implement fetch command logic in `cmd/lastfm-sync/commands/fetch.go`
  - Parse config from flags (viper integration)
  - Validate required fields (LASTFM_API_KEY, --user)
  - Create Last.fm client, LocalWriter, FileStore
  - Main fetch loop:
    - Load watermark for user
    - Calculate effective lower bound: `max(--since, watermark)`
    - Pagination loop: fetch page → transform → write batch → update watermark
    - Check short-circuit (0 records with uts > watermark)
    - Exit on completion

- [ ] T042 [US1] Implement structured logging in fetch flow `internal/logging/logger.go` + fetch command
  - Log events: fetch.start, fetch.page, fetch.write, watermark.update, fetch.complete
  - Track metrics: pages_fetched, records_written, bytes_written, total_duration

- [ ] T043 [US1] Add error handling and user messages
  - Clear error messages on API key missing, invalid user, file permission denied
  - Exit codes: 0 on success, 1 on failure

- [ ] T044 [US1] Implement --dry-run mode
  - Preview what would be fetched without making API calls or writing
  - Log: "Would fetch X pages, Y records to {output_path}"

**Checkpoint**: User Story 1 complete. User can fetch full history to local file. P1 MVP foundation ready.

