## Phase 4: User Story 2 - Incremental Sync with Watermarking (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: Subsequent runs fetch only new scrobbles since last sync; watermark-based idempotent resumption

**Independent Test**: First run fetches all → second run (with new API data) fetches only delta → verify no duplicates

### Tests for User Story 2 (TDD: Write First)

- [ ] T045 [P] [US2] Unit test: Watermark logic in `internal/lastfm/client_test.go`
  - Test effective lower bound: `max(--since, watermark)`
  - Test watermark override with --since flag
  - Test short-circuit on zero new records

- [ ] T046 [P] [US2] Unit test: Idempotency check in `internal/writer/local_test.go`
  - Write same batch twice → verify no duplicates in file
  - Verify uniqueness by (username, uts, artist, track)

- [ ] T047 [US2] Integration test: Incremental sync flow in `cmd/lastfm-sync/integration_test.go`
  - Run 1: Mock API returns pages 1-3 (uts 100-300)
  - Verify watermark = 300
  - Run 2: Mock API returns pages 1-2 (uts 100-200) + pages 3-5 (new, uts 301-500)
  - Verify only pages 3-5 fetched (effective_from = 300)
  - Verify output file has 600 total records (no duplicates)
  - Verify watermark = 500

- [ ] T048 [US2] Integration test: Crash recovery in `cmd/lastfm-sync/integration_test.go`
  - Simulate process kill after page 1 written but before watermark update
  - Rerun: verify page 1 records NOT duplicated (watermark still at 0)
  - Verify correct recovery from page 1

### Implementation for User Story 2

- [ ] T049 [US2] Enhance LastfmClient.FetchPage to accept `from` (watermark-based lower bound)
  - Pass as `from` parameter to Last.fm API
  - Unit tests: from parameter correctly set

- [ ] T050 [US2] Enhance fetch command to load and use watermark `cmd/lastfm-sync/commands/fetch.go`
  - Load watermark before pagination loop
  - Calculate: `effective_from = max(--since flag, watermark.max_uts)`
  - Pass to FetchPage

- [ ] T051 [US2] Implement short-circuit in pagination loop
  - After each page: check if `0 records with uts > current watermark`
  - If true: exit pagination (no need to fetch earlier pages)
  - Unit + integration tests

- [ ] T052 [US2] Implement atomic watermark updates in fetch loop
  - Update watermark after each successfully flushed page (not at end)
  - Use atomic writes to prevent corruption on crash
  - Verify in integration test: kill after write, before watermark update → correct recovery

- [ ] T053 [US2] Add --since flag validation and interaction with watermark
  - If both --since and watermark present: use max
  - Test all combinations

**Checkpoint**: User Story 2 complete. Incremental sync working with crash-safe watermarks. Full P1 MVP ready.

