## Phase 5: User Story 3 - Azure Blob Storage Output (Priority: P2)

**Goal**: User can write scrobbles to Azure Blob Storage with time-partitioned paths and managed identity auth

**Independent Test**: Mock Azure (Azurite) → run fetch with --output azure → verify blob structure and watermark

### Tests for User Story 3 (TDD: Write First)

- [ ] T054 [P] [US3] Unit test: Azure blob path formatting in `internal/writer/azure_test.go`
  - Test path construction: `{prefix}dt=YYYY-MM-DD/{username}-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.ndjson`
  - Verify date partitioning
  - Verify filename uniqueness (timestamp component)

- [ ] T055 [P] [US3] Unit test: AzureStore watermark in `internal/watermark/azure_test.go`
  - Test watermark blob path: `{prefix}{username}.watermark`
  - Mock ETag concurrency scenarios

- [ ] T056 [US3] Integration test: Azure end-to-end with Azurite in `cmd/lastfm-sync/integration_test.go`
  - Start Azurite container (managed by test framework)
  - Mock Last.fm API with 2 pages
  - Run `lastfm-sync fetch --user alice --output azure --azure-container test --azure-prefix lastfm/ --azure-auth default`
  - Verify blob created: `lastfm/dt=YYYY-MM-DD/alice-HHMMSS.ndjson`
  - Verify watermark blob created: `lastfm/alice.watermark`
  - Rerun: verify new blob created (not overwritten)

- [ ] T057 [US3] Integration test: Azure auth methods in `cmd/lastfm-sync/integration_test.go`
  - Test DefaultAzureCredential (mock)
  - Test connection string auth (with env var)
  - Test SAS token auth (with container URL + token env var)

### Implementation for User Story 3

- [ ] T058 Create `internal/config/azure.go` with Azure auth resolution
  - Parse `--azure-auth` flag (default, connstr, sas)
  - Create appropriate credential provider (DefaultAzureCredential, connection string, SAS)
  - Unit tests: credential selection logic

- [ ] T059 [P] [US3] Complete AzureWriter implementation in `internal/writer/azure.go`
  - Use local writer pattern for temp file buffering
  - `Flush()` → upload temp file to Azure with time-partitioned blob name
  - `Close()` → delete temp file on success, leave for debugging on error
  - Set Content-Type: `application/x-ndjson`
  - Unit + integration tests

- [ ] T060 [P] [US3] Complete AzureStore implementation in `internal/watermark/azure.go`
  - `Get()` → read watermark blob (handle not-found)
  - `Put()` → write watermark blob with ETag concurrency check (prevent concurrent writes)
  - Unit + integration tests with Azurite

- [ ] T061 [US3] Enhance fetch command to support Azure output in `cmd/lastfm-sync/commands/fetch.go`
  - Parse `--output azure` flag
  - Parse `--azure-container`, `--azure-prefix`, `--azure-auth`, `--azure-account`, `--azure-container-url`
  - Create AzureWriter + AzureStore based on auth method
  - Validate required Azure fields present
  - Unit + integration tests

- [ ] T062 [US3] Implement auto-watermark-store selection
  - If `--output azure` and `--watermark-store` not specified: auto-use azure
  - If `--output local` and `--watermark-store` not specified: use file
  - Allow explicit override via `--watermark-store` flag

- [ ] T063 [US3] Add Azure secret redaction in logging
  - Redact connection strings and SAS tokens as `****last4`
  - Test in unit tests

**Checkpoint**: User Story 3 complete. Azure Blob output with incremental sync. Cloud integration ready.

