## Phase 6: User Story 4 - Rate Limit Compliance and Backoff (Priority: P2)

**Goal**: Respect Last.fm 3 QPS limit; automatic exponential backoff on 429/5xx; no API bans

**Independent Test**: Throttle to 3 QPS → verify requests take ≥ 30s for 100 calls; mock 429 → verify backoff

### Tests for User Story 4 (TDD: Write First)

- [ ] T064 [P] [US4] Unit test: Rate limiter QPS enforcement in `internal/ratelimit/limiter_test.go`
  - Create limiter with QPS=3
  - Make 10 requests
  - Measure time elapsed
  - Verify: time ≥ 3.33 seconds (10 requests / 3 QPS)

- [ ] T065 [P] [US4] Unit test: Exponential backoff sequence in `internal/ratelimit/backoff_test.go`
  - Test backoff sequence: 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s, 32s (capped)
  - Verify max retries enforced
  - Verify jitter optional (no jitter for deterministic tests)

- [ ] T066 [P] [US4] Unit test: Retry-After header parsing in `internal/ratelimit/backoff_test.go`
  - Parse Retry-After: 60 → use 60s instead of backoff sequence
  - Verify fallback to backoff if header missing

- [ ] T067 [US4] Unit test: Retryable error classification in `internal/ratelimit/backoff_test.go`
  - 429 → retryable
  - 5xx → retryable
  - 4xx (except 429) → not retryable
  - network timeout → retryable

- [ ] T068 [US4] Integration test: 429 retry flow in `cmd/lastfm-sync/integration_test.go`
  - Mock Last.fm API: return 429 for first 2 requests, then 200
  - Run fetch
  - Verify retry occurred (check logs for retry events)
  - Verify request succeeded after backoff

- [ ] T069 [US4] Integration test: 5xx retry flow in `cmd/lastfm-sync/integration_test.go`
  - Mock Last.fm API: return 503 for first request, then 200
  - Run fetch
  - Verify retry occurred, succeeded after backoff

### Implementation for User Story 4

- [ ] T070 [P] [US4] Enhance Last.fm client to use rate limiter in `internal/lastfm/client.go`
  - Integrate `ratelimit.Limiter` with `DoWithRetry`
  - Every HTTP request calls `limiter.Wait(ctx)` before executing
  - Test with mocked limiter

- [ ] T071 [P] [US4] Implement Retry-After header parsing in `internal/ratelimit/backoff.go`
  - Extract `Retry-After` header from response
  - Use specified duration if present, else exponential backoff

- [ ] T072 [US4] Add --qps and --timeout flags to fetch command `cmd/lastfm-sync/commands/fetch.go`
  - `--qps` flag (default 3) → passed to rate limiter
  - `--timeout` flag (default 15s) → passed to HTTP client

- [ ] T073 [US4] Implement timeout enforcement in Last.fm client `internal/lastfm/client.go`
  - Set `http.Client.Timeout` from config
  - Verify timeout errors are retryable
  - Unit tests: timeout triggers retry

- [ ] T074 [US4] Add retry metrics to logging `internal/logging/logger.go` + fetch command
  - Log `retry` event with attempt number, reason (429/5xx/timeout), backoff duration
  - Track `retries_total`, `rate_limit_hits` counters

- [ ] T075 [US4] Verify Last.fm API compliance
  - Ensure no excessive requests (manual testing against real API if possible)
  - Document QPS calculation: 3 QPS → 1 request per 333ms

**Checkpoint**: User Story 4 complete. Rate limiting and resilience production-ready.

