## Phase 8: Shared Testing & Quality Gates

**Purpose**: Cross-cutting test suite, performance benchmarks, code quality

### Comprehensive Testing

- [ ] T083 [P] Integration test: Config loading from file `cmd/lastfm-sync/integration_test.go`
  - Create `config.yaml` with test values
  - Load via `--config-path`
  - Verify flags > env > file priority
  - Test env var override of config file

- [ ] T084 [P] Integration test: Help and version commands in `cmd/lastfm-sync/integration_test.go`
  - Run `lastfm-sync --help` → show usage
  - Run `lastfm-sync version` → show build info
  - Run `lastfm-sync fetch --help` → show fetch-specific options

- [ ] T085 [P] Performance benchmark: NDJSON write throughput in `internal/writer/bench_test.go`
  - Benchmark writing 10K scrobbles
  - Target: > 200 scrobbles/sec
  - Measure CPU, memory usage

- [ ] T086 [P] Performance benchmark: Rate limiter overhead in `internal/ratelimit/bench_test.go`
  - Benchmark DoWithRetry with 1000 success calls (no retries)
  - Target: < 1ms overhead per call

- [ ] T087 [P] Linting and code quality checks
  - Run `make lint` → golangci-lint passes with strict rules
  - Run `go test -race ./...` → no race conditions detected
  - Verify coverage report: ≥ 80% overall, ≥ 90% critical packages (lastfm, watermark, writer)

- [ ] T088 [P] Contract tests for data structures in `internal/lastfm/models_test.go`, `internal/writer/writer_test.go`
  - Verify NDJSON scrobble record has all required fields
  - Verify watermark JSON structure correct
